# Copilot CLI. Its model endpoint doubles as its GitHub MCP server (/mcp on the same host), a
# write path to the forge that opacity cannot separate from model traffic — the trade SECURITY.md
# prices under "The web reached through the model provider".
# Model traffic goes to whichever of the four the token exchange below names for the account's
# plan; the first is the generic host, and the MCP server.
+host api.githubcopilot.com unrestricted
+host api.individual.githubcopilot.com unrestricted  # individual plan
+host api.business.githubcopilot.com unrestricted    # business plan
+host api.enterprise.githubcopilot.com unrestricted  # enterprise plan

# The two forge hosts stay TLS-inspected here as in the catalog: this file is what
# deny-unless-model admits for copilot, and it must not admit git push.
+host github.com allow=github-login-device  # device-flow sign-in: the allowance's two POSTs
+host api.github.com                        # Copilot token exchange, GET /copilot_internal/v2/token
